WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.030 --> 00:00:03.290
I do as they tell me
and the street is safe.

2
00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:04.300
Who are "they"?

3
00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:06.400
I never meant for anyone
to get hurt.

4
00:00:06.510 --> 00:00:07.710
(RAVEN CAWS)

5
00:00:07.710 --> 00:00:09.580
(WHISPERS) Let me be brave.

6
00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:12.350
Is it a trap?
Is it a torture chamber?

7
00:00:12.350 --> 00:00:16.350
If you were
any part of killing her
and you're not afraid.

8
00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:18.620
then you understand
nothing at all.

9
00:00:22.790 --> 00:00:26.490
DOCTOR: <i>Go to the city.
tell them I'm back.</i>

10
00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:29.390
<i>Tell them I know what they did.</i>

11
00:01:14.210 --> 00:01:15.580
(DOOR CLOSES)

12
00:01:22.550 --> 00:01:23.990
Hi.

13
00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:27.010
What can I get you?

14
00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:30.090
I don't have any money.

15
00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:31.690
But I play.

16
00:01:33.390 --> 00:01:34.590
OK.

17
00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:41.190
Don't you need to
plug that thing in?

18
00:01:42.440 --> 00:01:44.240
Yeah.

19
00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:47.110
(GLASSES WHIRRING)

20
00:01:48.110 --> 00:01:49.510
You're English.

21
00:01:50.380 --> 00:01:51.750
You're not?

22
00:01:53.080 --> 00:01:54.650
How did you get out here?

23
00:01:54.650 --> 00:01:56.220
Magic.

24
00:01:56.420 --> 00:02:00.320
Or maybe I went to an airport
and caught a plane.

25
00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:02.620
- Ah. (CHUCKLES)
- You?

26
00:02:04.490 --> 00:02:05.760
Magic.

27
00:02:06.460 --> 00:02:09.060
(GUITAR PLAYS
OVER SPEAKERS)

28
00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:14.470
I believe you.

29
00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:20.470
- You been travelling?
- Yeah.

30
00:02:20.470 --> 00:02:22.530
From time to time.

31
00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:32.280
Is it a sad song?

32
00:02:32.380 --> 00:02:34.980
Nothing's sad till it's over...

33
00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:37.320
then. everything is.

34
00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:43.360
What's it called?

35
00:02:46.170 --> 00:02:48.230
I think that it's called...

36
00:02:48.230 --> 00:02:49.730
<i>Clara.</i>

37
00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:52.540
Tell me about her.

38
00:02:54.570 --> 00:02:57.240
(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)

39
00:03:58.140 --> 00:04:00.510
(WIND WHISTLING)

40
00:04:16.190 --> 00:04:17.560
Lord President.

41
00:04:17.560 --> 00:04:22.060
Are all the bells ringing?
The whole Cloister?

42
00:04:22.060 --> 00:04:24.060
What's going on down there?

43
00:04:24.060 --> 00:04:26.020
(BELLS TOLLING)

44
00:04:26.030 --> 00:04:28.490
GASTRON: <i>I'm on my way
down to the Matrix now. sir.</i>

45
00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:29.640
GENERAL: <i>Keep the perimeter.</i>

46
00:04:29.640 --> 00:04:31.740
<i>It's OK to be afraid
down there. soldier.</i>

47
00:04:31.740 --> 00:04:33.540
Sliders are everywhere. sir.

48
00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:34.280
Loads of those things.

49
00:04:34.270 --> 00:04:36.300
GENERAL: <i>Language. please.
I'm with the President.</i>

50
00:04:36.310 --> 00:04:39.580
Sorry. sir.
The Cloister Wraiths
are active.

51
00:04:39.580 --> 00:04:40.310
Do not approach them.

52
00:04:40.310 --> 00:04:42.340
Don't even enter the Cloister.
Just tell me.

53
00:04:42.350 --> 00:04:44.320
<i>Are all the bells ringing?</i>

54
00:04:44.320 --> 00:04:45.190
Yes. sir.

55
00:04:45.190 --> 00:04:47.750
Then we are facing great danger.

56
00:04:47.750 --> 00:04:50.510
The Cloister Wraiths
seem to think so.

57
00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:52.550
So where is he?

58
00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:53.590
Where has the Doctor gone?

59
00:04:53.590 --> 00:04:56.450
Back to the beginning.
I should think.

60
00:04:56.460 --> 00:05:00.290
The Sisterhood of Karn has
no business in this chamber

61
00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:01.000
or on this planet.

62
00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:03.970
I heard the Doctor
had come home.

63
00:05:03.970 --> 00:05:05.970
One so loves fireworks.

64
00:05:05.970 --> 00:05:07.600
(SCOFFS)

65
00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:44.110
Why are they
ringing all the bells?

66
00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:45.540
Never heard so many.

67
00:05:45.540 --> 00:05:47.140
What's gone wrong this time?

68
00:05:47.150 --> 00:05:50.280
All the fuss
they're always making.

69
00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:52.680
You up there. you're
not supposed to be there.

70
00:05:52.690 --> 00:05:55.660
I've just put all that back.
it's for the boys.

71
00:05:55.660 --> 00:05:58.420
If any of them
ever want to come...

72
00:06:08.470 --> 00:06:10.400
They'll kill you.

73
00:06:24.720 --> 00:06:26.650
(SPOON TINKLES)

74
00:06:38.100 --> 00:06:39.730
(SPACECRAFT APPROACHING)

75
00:06:54.780 --> 00:06:55.680
GASTRON: (ON PA) <i>Attention.</i>

76
00:06:55.680 --> 00:06:59.310
<i>All non-military personnel
step away from the Doctor.</i>

77
00:07:04.120 --> 00:07:04.550
I repeat.

78
00:07:04.560 --> 00:07:09.530
all non-military personnel
please step away
from the Doctor.

79
00:07:09.730 --> 00:07:12.500
<i>At least. move
the children away.</i>

80
00:07:14.030 --> 00:07:17.600
Doctor. you lay down
any weapons on your person.

81
00:07:17.600 --> 00:07:20.330
and accompany us to the Capitol.

82
00:07:41.630 --> 00:07:45.030
<i>Doctor. you will
accompany us to the Capitol.</i>

83
00:08:03.380 --> 00:08:05.210
<i>Doctor?</i>

84
00:08:08.120 --> 00:08:09.220
Come back.

85
00:08:09.220 --> 00:08:10.410
You will come back immediately.

86
00:08:10.420 --> 00:08:14.590
<i>That is an order. And
this is a military vehicle.</i>

87
00:08:21.630 --> 00:08:23.160
What's his plan?

88
00:08:23.170 --> 00:08:26.170
I think he's finishing his soup.

89
00:08:27.310 --> 00:08:29.480
- Suggestion. sir.
- Mmm.

90
00:08:29.480 --> 00:08:31.580
GENERAL: <i>We could talk to him.</i>

91
00:08:31.580 --> 00:08:33.980
RASSILON: <i>Words
are his weapons.</i>

92
00:08:33.980 --> 00:08:37.650
GENERAL: <i>When did
they stop being ours?</i>

93
00:08:43.120 --> 00:08:45.050
(KNOCK ON DOOR)

94
00:09:08.650 --> 00:09:10.320
Welcome home. sir.

95
00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:13.020
As commander of the
armed forces of Gallifrey.

96
00:09:13.020 --> 00:09:16.390
- I bring you the
greetings of the...
-(DOOR CREAKING)

97
00:09:16.390 --> 00:09:17.930
High Council.

98
00:09:23.060 --> 00:09:26.020
<i>Who the hell
does he think he is?</i>

99
00:09:26.030 --> 00:09:28.490
The man who won
the Time War. sir.

100
00:09:33.510 --> 00:09:35.440
(KNOCK ON DOOR)

101
00:09:55.490 --> 00:09:57.560
What is he doing?

102
00:10:03.170 --> 00:10:05.240
What does he want?

103
00:10:06.240 --> 00:10:06.770
Revenge?

104
00:10:06.770 --> 00:10:08.670
The Doctor does
not blame Gallifrey

105
00:10:08.670 --> 00:10:11.040
for the horrors of the Time War.

106
00:10:11.040 --> 00:10:13.100
I should hope not.

107
00:10:13.110 --> 00:10:16.110
He just blames you.

108
00:10:22.090 --> 00:10:23.590
(KNOCKING ON DOOR)

109
00:10:23.990 --> 00:10:26.490
(BREATHING SHAKILY)

110
00:11:26.050 --> 00:11:28.180
Get off my planet.

111
00:11:29.690 --> 00:11:31.760
We needed to know.

112
00:11:32.190 --> 00:11:35.160
You have information
about the Hybrid.

113
00:11:35.160 --> 00:11:37.300
a danger to all of us.

114
00:11:37.300 --> 00:11:38.430
If you told us what you knew.

115
00:11:38.430 --> 00:11:40.100
you could have
walked out of there.

116
00:11:40.100 --> 00:11:42.470
Get off my planet.

117
00:11:44.500 --> 00:11:48.270
You have nothing.
Doctor. Nothing!

118
00:11:48.740 --> 00:11:50.380
Do you know what
I have out here.

119
00:11:50.380 --> 00:11:55.180
in the dry lands. where
there's nobody who matters?

120
00:11:55.180 --> 00:11:57.750
(WHISPERING) No witnesses.

121
00:11:59.220 --> 00:12:00.820
Me. too.

122
00:12:02.450 --> 00:12:04.010
Take aim!

123
00:12:04.760 --> 00:12:06.730
Aim at the Doctor.

124
00:12:09.130 --> 00:12:10.560
Fire on my command.

125
00:12:10.560 --> 00:12:11.690
Sir...

126
00:12:11.700 --> 00:12:13.130
RASSILON: Step forward.

127
00:12:13.130 --> 00:12:16.130
And take aim.
What's the matter with you?

128
00:12:16.130 --> 00:12:19.700
Lord President. he's a war hero.

129
00:12:19.710 --> 00:12:22.010
Some of these men
served with him.

130
00:12:22.010 --> 00:12:24.080
These men serve me!

131
00:12:25.310 --> 00:12:26.750
All of you!

132
00:12:27.150 --> 00:12:29.620
(GUNS POWERING UP)

133
00:12:30.720 --> 00:12:33.120
On my command.

134
00:12:49.530 --> 00:12:51.330
Fire!

135
00:12:55.170 --> 00:12:57.200
DOCTOR: <i>Could I
have a lemonade?</i>

136
00:12:57.540 --> 00:13:01.140
Oh. You like
a cliff-hanger. don't you?

137
00:13:03.180 --> 00:13:05.740
So. you went back
to your hometown.

138
00:13:05.750 --> 00:13:07.540
Something like that.

139
00:13:07.550 --> 00:13:08.680
Glasgow?

140
00:13:08.690 --> 00:13:10.490
Uh... Well. sort of Glasgow.

141
00:13:10.490 --> 00:13:11.290
Space Glasgow.

142
00:13:11.290 --> 00:13:14.360
And there's this gang boss.
and he wanted to kill you?

143
00:13:15.190 --> 00:13:17.190
Wanted to. Yeah.

144
00:13:33.750 --> 00:13:35.680
You missed.

145
00:13:36.450 --> 00:13:39.080
All of you.
every single one of you.

146
00:13:39.080 --> 00:13:41.150
How is that possible?

147
00:13:41.390 --> 00:13:42.290
What is it?

148
00:13:42.290 --> 00:13:46.490
Is the firing squad afraid
of the unarmed man?

149
00:13:48.560 --> 00:13:50.500
You. explain.

150
00:13:51.260 --> 00:13:54.160
There was a saying.
sir. in the Time War.

151
00:13:54.170 --> 00:13:54.770
"A saying"?

152
00:13:54.770 --> 00:13:59.070
GASTRON:
First thing you notice about
the Doctor of War...

153
00:13:59.540 --> 00:14:01.340
is he's unarmed.

154
00:14:01.570 --> 00:14:04.270
For many. it's also the last.

155
00:14:27.530 --> 00:14:29.690
I was at Skaro Moon. sir.

156
00:14:32.200 --> 00:14:34.400
Is this a story.
or did this really happen?

157
00:14:34.410 --> 00:14:38.080
Every story I ever told
really happened.

158
00:14:39.180 --> 00:14:40.580
Stories...

159
00:14:40.580 --> 00:14:43.580
are where memories go
when they're forgotten.

160
00:14:50.190 --> 00:14:54.130
Not one more of you moves.
That is an order.

161
00:14:54.190 --> 00:14:57.650
A direct order
of your president!

162
00:15:01.230 --> 00:15:03.730
You leave me no choice.

163
00:15:04.640 --> 00:15:08.140
How many regenerations
did we grant you?

164
00:15:08.140 --> 00:15:12.480
- I've got all night.
- (SPACECRAFTS APPROACHING)

165
00:15:14.150 --> 00:15:17.650
Excellent. General.
you sent for reinforcements.

166
00:15:17.650 --> 00:15:19.450
DOCTOR: No. he didn't.

167
00:15:22.420 --> 00:15:24.120
I did.

168
00:15:34.470 --> 00:15:39.240
I am Rassilon. the redeemer.

169
00:15:40.510 --> 00:15:43.240
Rassilon. the resurrected.

170
00:15:43.310 --> 00:15:46.580
Gallifrey is mine!

171
00:15:47.710 --> 00:15:52.210
Lord President. with respect.

172
00:15:52.620 --> 00:15:55.160
get off his planet.

173
00:16:14.070 --> 00:16:15.470
GENERAL: Gallifrey is
currently positioned

174
00:16:15.470 --> 00:16:21.170
at the extreme end
of the time continuum
for its own protection.

175
00:16:21.350 --> 00:16:22.750
We're the end of the universe.

176
00:16:22.750 --> 00:16:24.450
give or take a star system.

177
00:16:24.450 --> 00:16:28.620
I know. I came
the long way around.

178
00:16:29.520 --> 00:16:33.180
The President may not
find anywhere to go.

179
00:16:35.730 --> 00:16:38.600
He's not the president any more.

180
00:16:38.660 --> 00:16:41.190
He was a good man once.

181
00:16:41.200 --> 00:16:44.170
Isn't this going a little far?

182
00:16:44.170 --> 00:16:46.470
Oh. I've barely started.

183
00:16:46.470 --> 00:16:50.470
Tell the High Council
they're on the next shuttle.

184
00:17:05.090 --> 00:17:10.160
OHILA: I thought I'd
find you down here.
Old times.

185
00:17:12.960 --> 00:17:13.920
You're a long way from Karn.

186
00:17:13.930 --> 00:17:16.260
At the end of everything.
one must expect

187
00:17:16.270 --> 00:17:19.010
the company of immortals.

188
00:17:19.200 --> 00:17:21.300
Do you know what they did to me?

189
00:17:21.310 --> 00:17:24.080
Confession dial is
a ritual act of purification.

190
00:17:24.080 --> 00:17:25.110
It allows a dying Time Lord

191
00:17:25.110 --> 00:17:27.410
to face his demons
and make his peace.

192
00:17:27.410 --> 00:17:30.670
before his mind
is uploaded to the Matrix.

193
00:17:30.680 --> 00:17:34.010
It was never intended
as a torture chamber
for the living!

194
00:17:34.020 --> 00:17:38.960
Rassilon grew concerned about
the coming of the Hybrid.

195
00:17:38.960 --> 00:17:39.260
Afraid.

196
00:17:39.260 --> 00:17:42.360
You were entrapped and
imprisoned at his command.

197
00:17:42.360 --> 00:17:45.430
- And look at him now.
- Why did you banish him?

198
00:17:45.430 --> 00:17:48.540
Was it punishment.
or for your own protection?

199
00:17:48.540 --> 00:17:53.960
We're you just being cruel
or just being cowardly?

200
00:17:53.970 --> 00:17:56.130
Let's see. shall we?

201
00:17:56.140 --> 00:17:58.500
If you wanted to
know about the Hybrid.
why didn't you just ask me?

202
00:17:58.510 --> 00:18:04.380
If the Hybrid is a threat
to the people of this world.
why don't you just tell us?

203
00:18:04.380 --> 00:18:06.210
What do you know already?

204
00:18:07.420 --> 00:18:09.920
- The Hybrid is a legendary...
- No.

205
00:18:10.320 --> 00:18:15.550
The Hybrid is a creature
thought to be cross-bred
from two warrior races.

206
00:18:15.560 --> 00:18:16.530
Which races?

207
00:18:16.530 --> 00:18:19.030
The Daleks and the Time Lords.
It is supposed...

208
00:18:19.030 --> 00:18:20.630
Oh. it must be well hard then.

209
00:18:20.630 --> 00:18:24.160
Unstoppable.
according to the stories.

210
00:18:24.170 --> 00:18:27.370
If they're just stories.
why are you so worried?

211
00:18:27.370 --> 00:18:30.330
Some Matrix
prophecies suggest...

212
00:18:30.340 --> 00:18:32.140
No.

213
00:18:33.950 --> 00:18:35.980
Many prophecies suggest...

214
00:18:35.980 --> 00:18:37.620
No.

215
00:18:40.120 --> 00:18:43.120
All Matrix prophecies concur

216
00:18:43.120 --> 00:18:45.550
that this creature will one day

217
00:18:45.560 --> 00:18:48.160
stand in the ruins of Gallifrey.

218
00:18:48.160 --> 00:18:49.600
It will unravel the web of time.

219
00:18:49.600 --> 00:18:53.990
and destroy a billion billion
hearts to heal his own.

220
00:18:54.000 --> 00:18:55.740
What colour is it?

221
00:18:57.200 --> 00:18:57.630
I don't know.

222
00:18:57.640 --> 00:19:00.340
These prophecies.
they never tell you
anything useful. do they?

223
00:19:00.340 --> 00:19:01.910
This is no time
to play the fool.

224
00:19:01.910 --> 00:19:04.910
It's the end of the universe.
it's the only time I've got!

225
00:19:04.910 --> 00:19:06.910
And you want me
to keep you all safe?

226
00:19:06.910 --> 00:19:10.270
- Can you?
- I'll need help. obviously.

227
00:19:10.280 --> 00:19:11.140
Gallifrey is at your command.

228
00:19:11.150 --> 00:19:14.290
Well. not from you lot.
No. you'd cramp my style.

229
00:19:14.290 --> 00:19:15.620
Look at your hats.

230
00:19:15.620 --> 00:19:23.560
I'm going to need the use
of an extraction chamber
to talk to an old friend.

231
00:19:32.640 --> 00:19:34.010
(RAVEN CAWS)

232
00:19:34.010 --> 00:19:36.040
(WHISPERS) Let me be brave.

233
00:19:37.640 --> 00:19:39.440
(THUD)

234
00:19:45.280 --> 00:19:47.410
(EXHALES SHARPLY)

235
00:19:52.990 --> 00:19:56.590
This way. I can save you.

236
00:20:18.580 --> 00:20:19.640
- Doctor?
- DOCTOR: Yeah.

237
00:20:19.650 --> 00:20:22.250
Where am I?
Is this the Tardis?

238
00:20:22.250 --> 00:20:24.110
DOCTOR: No. this is a planet.

239
00:20:24.120 --> 00:20:25.020
CLARA: What planet?

240
00:20:25.020 --> 00:20:28.250
- Basically. my place.
- I was about to die.

241
00:20:28.260 --> 00:20:29.630
I should be dead.

242
00:20:29.630 --> 00:20:31.660
DOCTOR: Forget about that.
It doesn't matter.

243
00:20:31.660 --> 00:20:33.160
- Hang on. Your place?
- Yeah.

244
00:20:33.160 --> 00:20:34.420
- What do you
mean your place?
- My place.

245
00:20:34.430 --> 00:20:36.990
- CLARA: You don't mean...
- Yeah.

246
00:20:37.000 --> 00:20:38.360
Gallifrey.

247
00:20:38.370 --> 00:20:40.310
Gallifrey.

248
00:20:40.310 --> 00:20:43.310
OK. Uh...
Hang on. Wait. What?

249
00:20:43.310 --> 00:20:44.680
What? Did I miss something?

250
00:20:44.680 --> 00:20:46.680
Well. we're several billion
years in the future

251
00:20:46.680 --> 00:20:48.580
and the universe
is pretty much over.

252
00:20:48.580 --> 00:20:49.350
so. yeah. quite a lot.

253
00:20:49.350 --> 00:20:51.220
GENERAL: Young lady.
Miss Oswald.

254
00:20:51.220 --> 00:20:54.620
I'm afraid we only have
very few minutes with you.

255
00:20:57.490 --> 00:20:58.090
Who's he?

256
00:20:58.090 --> 00:21:00.090
According to the Doctor.
you can tell us something

257
00:21:00.090 --> 00:21:02.520
about the creature
known as the Hybrid.

258
00:21:02.530 --> 00:21:03.360
Ah. Ooh.

259
00:21:03.360 --> 00:21:05.220
Well. that's weird.
What's wrong with my ears?

260
00:21:05.230 --> 00:21:08.400
- DOCTOR: Nothing.
- Ooh. it's weird.
Everything sounds wrong.

261
00:21:08.400 --> 00:21:10.200
- DOCTOR: It's a side effect.
- I can hear you.

262
00:21:10.200 --> 00:21:11.360
- I can hear you fine.
- DOCTOR: Uh-huh.

263
00:21:11.370 --> 00:21:13.710
But I don't know.
It's like. um...

264
00:21:13.710 --> 00:21:14.740
It's like something's missing.

265
00:21:14.740 --> 00:21:17.610
Doctor. we have to tell her.
we always tell them.

266
00:21:17.610 --> 00:21:21.580
Tell me what? What's he
talking about? Doctor?

267
00:21:26.780 --> 00:21:29.010
Doctor. what's going on?

268
00:21:29.520 --> 00:21:30.460
DOCTOR: Clara. there's a sound

269
00:21:30.460 --> 00:21:32.430
you've been living with
every day of your life.

270
00:21:32.430 --> 00:21:35.320
that you've learnt not to hear.

271
00:21:36.530 --> 00:21:37.660
What sound?

272
00:21:37.660 --> 00:21:40.660
(CHUCKLES NERVOUSLY)
What's wrong? Just tell me.

273
00:21:40.730 --> 00:21:42.330
Doctor. what sound?

274
00:21:42.330 --> 00:21:43.990
Your heartbeat.

275
00:21:46.170 --> 00:21:49.710
Your physical processes
have been time looped.

276
00:21:50.510 --> 00:21:55.250
Frozen between one
heartbeat and the next.

277
00:21:56.110 --> 00:21:58.540
Even your breathing
is just a habit.

278
00:21:59.280 --> 00:22:01.280
You don't need it.

279
00:22:04.320 --> 00:22:07.250
If I'm frozen. how can I...

280
00:22:07.260 --> 00:22:08.730
How can I be walking about?

281
00:22:08.730 --> 00:22:11.100
Because the Time Lords
are very clever.

282
00:22:11.100 --> 00:22:13.730
- It doesn't matter...
- Yes. it matters to me.

283
00:22:13.730 --> 00:22:16.090
Doctor. we have to explain.

284
00:22:16.100 --> 00:22:16.970
Doctor. what is going on?

285
00:22:16.970 --> 00:22:19.170
GENERAL: Although. you are
currently conscious and aware.

286
00:22:19.170 --> 00:22:23.210
in fact. you died
billions of years ago.

287
00:22:23.340 --> 00:22:23.700
Doctor?

288
00:22:23.710 --> 00:22:28.210
We have extracted you at the
very end of your time stream

289
00:22:28.210 --> 00:22:28.770
to request your help.

290
00:22:28.780 --> 00:22:33.220
Once we're finished here.
you'll be returned to your
final moments.

291
00:22:33.220 --> 00:22:37.260
Your death is an
established historical event

292
00:22:37.260 --> 00:22:39.720
and cannot be altered.
I'm sorry.

293
00:22:39.720 --> 00:22:41.380
Doctor. will you
just talk to me?

294
00:22:41.390 --> 00:22:42.420
I'll try not to break your jaw.

295
00:22:42.430 --> 00:22:45.260
- My jaw?
- I wasn't talking to you.

296
00:22:45.260 --> 00:22:47.060
(GRUNTS)

297
00:22:48.200 --> 00:22:51.170
Doctor. you can't do this.
You know you can't.

298
00:22:51.170 --> 00:22:52.710
No. General. I don't know that.

299
00:22:52.710 --> 00:22:56.530
Everybody.
stay exactly where you are.

300
00:22:56.540 --> 00:22:57.270
No moving about.

301
00:22:57.280 --> 00:22:59.250
On pain of death.
no-one take a selfie.

302
00:22:59.250 --> 00:23:01.370
These people are unarmed.

303
00:23:01.380 --> 00:23:03.080
So are you.

304
00:23:03.080 --> 00:23:04.510
Doctor. I will not
let you leave here.

305
00:23:04.520 --> 00:23:09.520
That's the sidearm
of the president's
personal security.

306
00:23:09.520 --> 00:23:12.160
there isn't a stun setting.

307
00:23:12.560 --> 00:23:14.260
I will not let Clara die.

308
00:23:14.260 --> 00:23:17.700
She's been dead for half
the lifetime of the universe.

309
00:23:17.700 --> 00:23:22.070
If you try to change that.
you could fracture
time itself.

310
00:23:22.070 --> 00:23:26.640
Doctor. Lord President.
are you really gonna
take that risk?

311
00:23:30.480 --> 00:23:31.750
Doctor.

312
00:23:35.180 --> 00:23:36.980
Please.

313
00:23:39.080 --> 00:23:40.610
I don't want this.

314
00:23:43.350 --> 00:23:45.150
Put it down. please.

315
00:23:45.160 --> 00:23:46.760
Regeneration.

316
00:23:49.560 --> 00:23:51.130
Death.

317
00:23:51.560 --> 00:23:53.120
Good luck.

318
00:23:53.770 --> 00:23:56.100
- You too. sir.
- (GUNSHOT)

319
00:23:56.370 --> 00:23:58.040
I want a neural block.

320
00:23:58.040 --> 00:24:00.810
Human compatible.
Quickly. come on.

321
00:24:02.040 --> 00:24:03.980
Come on. Quick!

322
00:24:03.980 --> 00:24:07.710
This Clara person.
you must really like her.

323
00:24:08.210 --> 00:24:10.210
Why do you say that?

324
00:24:10.210 --> 00:24:11.740
You killed a man.

325
00:24:12.420 --> 00:24:13.950
You don't seem the type.

326
00:24:13.950 --> 00:24:17.610
CLARA: You killed that man.
You shot him. He's dead.

327
00:24:17.620 --> 00:24:19.620
- DOCTOR: It was him or you.
- I don't care!

328
00:24:19.620 --> 00:24:24.020
Yeah? Well. the difference is.
when you die. you stay dead.

329
00:24:24.030 --> 00:24:24.560
So does he.

330
00:24:24.560 --> 00:24:27.590
We're on Gallifrey.
Death is Time Lord
for man flu.

331
00:24:27.600 --> 00:24:31.040
Med Team to Sector 52.
extraction chamber seven.

332
00:24:31.040 --> 00:24:33.240
Regeneration in progress.

333
00:24:38.610 --> 00:24:41.050
Are you all right. sir?

334
00:24:43.450 --> 00:24:46.190
(STUTTERS) Uh. sorry. ma'am.

335
00:24:47.520 --> 00:24:49.320
(GRUNTS)

336
00:24:49.620 --> 00:24:51.290
Back to normal. am I?

337
00:24:51.290 --> 00:24:54.330
The only time I've been a man.
that last body.

338
00:24:54.330 --> 00:24:57.130
Dear Lord. how do you
cope with all that ego?

339
00:24:57.130 --> 00:24:58.430
Ma'am. where's the Doctor?

340
00:24:58.430 --> 00:25:01.670
The Cloisters.
Where else would he run?

341
00:25:01.670 --> 00:25:04.640
Except into the greatest
danger on Gallifrey.

342
00:25:04.640 --> 00:25:06.240
<i>The hell of the Time Lords.</i>

343
00:25:06.240 --> 00:25:09.570
I thought you said
Gallifrey was frozen
in another dimension.

344
00:25:09.570 --> 00:25:11.570
Well. they must have
unfrozen it and come back.

345
00:25:11.580 --> 00:25:15.680
- CLARA: How?
- I didn't ask.
It'd make them feel clever.

346
00:25:19.550 --> 00:25:22.090
- Happy?
- No.

347
00:25:22.090 --> 00:25:25.090
Tell me what a neural block is.

348
00:25:25.090 --> 00:25:27.160
DOCTOR: Never mind.

349
00:25:27.230 --> 00:25:28.090
This way.

350
00:25:28.090 --> 00:25:30.150
CLARA: What did you mean
"human compatible"?

351
00:25:30.160 --> 00:25:33.220
So. what was it.
the thing you took?

352
00:25:33.230 --> 00:25:36.630
There was only one way
to keep Clara safe.

353
00:25:36.730 --> 00:25:39.560
I had to wipe
some of her memory.

354
00:25:40.510 --> 00:25:42.210
Of what?

355
00:25:42.710 --> 00:25:44.310
Of me.

356
00:25:50.380 --> 00:25:54.310
Cloister Wraiths.
Sliders. we used to call them.

357
00:25:54.320 --> 00:25:55.590
They guard the Matrix.

358
00:25:55.590 --> 00:25:57.290
- We're safe here.
- Why?

359
00:25:57.290 --> 00:26:00.020
They only attack if you
make any attempt to leave.

360
00:26:00.020 --> 00:26:01.990
How long are we
planning to stay?

361
00:26:01.990 --> 00:26:04.350
Or actually. if you try to stay.

362
00:26:06.130 --> 00:26:09.170
You realise how well that
conversation went. right?

363
00:26:09.170 --> 00:26:11.470
I'm starting to. yeah. a bit.

364
00:26:15.110 --> 00:26:18.010
(SCREAMING)

365
00:26:21.710 --> 00:26:24.110
We need to block every exit
from the Cloisters.

366
00:26:24.120 --> 00:26:27.020
Every available man.
I need that place surrounded.

367
00:26:27.020 --> 00:26:30.090
No-one's ever made it
back out of the Cloisters.

368
00:26:30.090 --> 00:26:31.460
No quite no-one.

369
00:26:31.460 --> 00:26:32.660
DOCTOR:
This way. I'm fairly sure.

370
00:26:32.660 --> 00:26:34.960
According to the stories.
there's a secret way out.

371
00:26:34.960 --> 00:26:37.560
If you find it.
the Sliders let you go.

372
00:26:37.560 --> 00:26:42.490
DALEK: <i>Exterminate.</i>

373
00:26:42.970 --> 00:26:47.270
It's OK.
It's OK. Look at it.

374
00:26:47.270 --> 00:26:51.600
<i>Exterminate me.</i>

375
00:26:51.610 --> 00:26:52.350
Is it trapped?

376
00:26:52.350 --> 00:26:55.710
DOCTOR: Don't worry.
it's been neutralised.

377
00:26:56.010 --> 00:26:56.770
Those aren't vines.

378
00:26:56.780 --> 00:27:01.380
In your terms. they
are fibre optic cables.
alive and growing.

379
00:27:01.390 --> 00:27:03.590
We're inside the
biggest database in history.

380
00:27:03.590 --> 00:27:06.630
Sometimes. people are
stupid enough to break in.

381
00:27:06.630 --> 00:27:08.020
And?

382
00:27:08.590 --> 00:27:11.590
It's a database.
They get filed.

383
00:27:11.600 --> 00:27:17.640
<i>Exterminate...</i>

384
00:27:18.570 --> 00:27:19.070
<i>me.</i>

385
00:27:19.070 --> 00:27:21.940
Probably left over
from the Cloister Wars.

386
00:27:22.210 --> 00:27:24.410
There's nothing we can do.

387
00:27:24.710 --> 00:27:25.650
Come on.

388
00:27:25.650 --> 00:27:28.300
<i>Exterminate me!</i>

389
00:27:28.310 --> 00:27:32.480
<i>Exterminate me!</i>

390
00:27:32.650 --> 00:27:35.120
<i>Exterminate me!</i>

391
00:27:35.120 --> 00:27:37.060
(CLARA GASPS)

392
00:28:01.910 --> 00:28:03.610
Keep away from them.

393
00:28:04.050 --> 00:28:06.050
The Matrix can use
them as a defence.

394
00:28:06.050 --> 00:28:09.120
It means the secret exit
must be close.

395
00:28:12.990 --> 00:28:15.530
- What's to
defend in a crypt?
- It's not just a crypt.

396
00:28:15.530 --> 00:28:17.700
It's more like
a stone circuit board.

397
00:28:17.960 --> 00:28:19.160
This is the Matrix database.

398
00:28:19.160 --> 00:28:23.360
CLARA: Database?
What do you mean. "database"?

399
00:28:25.470 --> 00:28:27.540
- (WHISPERS) Oh.
- Oh?

400
00:28:27.540 --> 00:28:29.510
- Oh.
- Oh?

401
00:28:30.610 --> 00:28:31.580
Oh.

402
00:28:31.580 --> 00:28:33.480
Looks like the
primary service hatch.

403
00:28:33.480 --> 00:28:36.650
- Just have to
work out the key.
- Oh.

404
00:28:37.280 --> 00:28:42.580
When Time Lords die.
their minds are uploaded
to a thing called the Matrix.

405
00:28:42.590 --> 00:28:44.990
This structure.
it's like a living computer.

406
00:28:44.990 --> 00:28:50.160
It can predict the future.
Generate prophecies
out of algorithms.

407
00:28:50.330 --> 00:28:51.630
Ring the Cloister bells

408
00:28:51.630 --> 00:28:54.300
in the event of
impending catastrophe.

409
00:28:56.030 --> 00:29:01.360
The Sliders. they're just like
the guard dogs. the firewall.

410
00:29:01.370 --> 00:29:04.170
They're projections from
inside the Matrix itself.

411
00:29:04.180 --> 00:29:08.410
The dead manning
the battlements.

412
00:29:08.410 --> 00:29:10.670
Was I supposed to
understand any of that?

413
00:29:10.680 --> 00:29:12.280
The Time Lords
have got a big computer

414
00:29:12.280 --> 00:29:16.150
made of ghosts in a crypt
guarded by more ghosts.

415
00:29:16.150 --> 00:29:18.580
- Didn't hurt. did it?
- Tiny bit.

416
00:29:25.530 --> 00:29:27.360
Why would a computer
need to protect itself

417
00:29:27.360 --> 00:29:28.220
from the people who made it?

418
00:29:28.230 --> 00:29:29.530
DOCTOR: All computers
do that in the end.

419
00:29:29.530 --> 00:29:34.230
You wait
till the internet starts.
Oh. that was a war.

420
00:29:36.010 --> 00:29:37.680
GASTRON: They don't
seem to be moving.

421
00:29:37.680 --> 00:29:39.950
They're by lift shaft seven.

422
00:29:41.180 --> 00:29:42.580
Keep monitoring.

423
00:29:45.550 --> 00:29:48.450
Long time ago. there was
a student at the academy.

424
00:29:48.450 --> 00:29:49.710
he'd got in here.

425
00:29:49.720 --> 00:29:52.060
Disappeared for four days.

426
00:29:52.060 --> 00:29:55.330
Showed up in a completely
different part of the city.

427
00:29:55.330 --> 00:29:58.230
He said the Sliders
talked to him.

428
00:29:58.230 --> 00:30:01.100
They showed him
the secret passage out.

429
00:30:01.100 --> 00:30:02.300
We just need the code.

430
00:30:02.300 --> 00:30:03.970
What. and the kid
told you the secret?

431
00:30:03.970 --> 00:30:07.440
Ah. no. He didn't tell
anyone anything.
He went completely mad.

432
00:30:07.440 --> 00:30:09.510
Never right in the head again.
so they say.

433
00:30:09.510 --> 00:30:11.180
OK. that's encouraging.

434
00:30:11.180 --> 00:30:12.280
The last I heard.

435
00:30:12.280 --> 00:30:16.180
he stole the moon
and the President's wife.

436
00:30:19.080 --> 00:30:20.040
Was she. um...

437
00:30:20.050 --> 00:30:21.550
Was she nice.
the President's wife?

438
00:30:21.550 --> 00:30:24.010
Ah. well. that was a lie
put about by the Shebugans.

439
00:30:24.020 --> 00:30:26.350
-(BEEPING)
- It was
the President's daughter.

440
00:30:26.360 --> 00:30:29.030
I didn't steal the moon.
I lost...

441
00:30:30.330 --> 00:30:32.200
I'd know you anywhere.

442
00:30:33.530 --> 00:30:36.790
I was a completely different
person in those days.

443
00:30:36.800 --> 00:30:38.560
Eccentric. A bit mad!

444
00:30:38.570 --> 00:30:40.370
(CHUCKLES) Rude to people.

445
00:30:40.370 --> 00:30:42.470
- Look at me again.
- I'm sorry. what?

446
00:30:42.470 --> 00:30:46.270
In the eye. look at me.
Just do it.

447
00:30:46.710 --> 00:30:48.410
What...

448
00:30:49.810 --> 00:30:51.570
What is it?

449
00:30:53.080 --> 00:30:55.680
How long has it been for you
since you last saw me?

450
00:30:55.690 --> 00:30:57.220
Oh... (MUMBLES)

451
00:30:57.220 --> 00:30:59.280
- Well. I'm not sure.
- How long?

452
00:31:00.760 --> 00:31:02.630
I was stuck in a place.

453
00:31:03.430 --> 00:31:04.130
- They...
- They?

454
00:31:04.130 --> 00:31:06.030
What... Who...
Who are we talking about?

455
00:31:06.030 --> 00:31:09.040
They wanted something
from me... Information.

456
00:31:10.970 --> 00:31:13.070
It really doesn't matter.

457
00:31:17.470 --> 00:31:19.040
What happened to your coat?

458
00:31:19.040 --> 00:31:21.540
Velvety one? I liked that one.
It was...

459
00:31:21.550 --> 00:31:22.980
- It was very Doctor-ey...
- I changed it.

460
00:31:22.980 --> 00:31:26.250
- Why?
- Well. I can't be the Doctor
all the time.

461
00:31:26.250 --> 00:31:26.690
(BEEPING)

462
00:31:26.690 --> 00:31:30.050
I think I've almost got it.
I think this is it.

463
00:31:30.050 --> 00:31:31.750
Tell me what they did to you.

464
00:31:31.760 --> 00:31:34.560
Tell me what happened
to the Doctor?

465
00:31:36.990 --> 00:31:37.990
We're here.

466
00:31:38.000 --> 00:31:40.060
Looks pretty quiet.

467
00:31:40.060 --> 00:31:42.020
<i>He seems to be talking to her.</i>

468
00:31:42.030 --> 00:31:44.130
<i>Like he's telling her a story.</i>

469
00:31:44.130 --> 00:31:46.030
<i>You might want to have a look.</i>

470
00:31:46.040 --> 00:31:47.170
Open up. We're going in.

471
00:31:47.170 --> 00:31:50.770
We'll stick to the perimeter.
No more than three paces
from the lift.

472
00:31:50.770 --> 00:31:52.340
Do not enter the Cloisters.

473
00:31:52.340 --> 00:31:56.540
DOCTOR: Twenty feet
of pure diamond.
Harder than diamond.

474
00:31:56.550 --> 00:31:57.380
(DOOR OPENS)

475
00:31:57.380 --> 00:32:00.240
But you'll break through
anything. given time.

476
00:32:00.480 --> 00:32:01.140
CLARA: How much time?

477
00:32:01.150 --> 00:32:03.150
- FEMALE GENERAL: Miss Oswald.
- Stay back.

478
00:32:03.150 --> 00:32:05.680
I'm sorry. But we have
to find a way...

479
00:32:05.690 --> 00:32:08.390
I said stay back!

480
00:32:15.270 --> 00:32:16.970
The Hybrid. What is it?

481
00:32:16.970 --> 00:32:18.570
What's so important
you would fight so long?

482
00:32:18.570 --> 00:32:19.740
It doesn't matter
what the Hybrid is.

483
00:32:19.740 --> 00:32:22.270
It only matters that I
convinced them that I knew.

484
00:32:22.270 --> 00:32:23.500
Otherwise. they would
have kicked me out

485
00:32:23.510 --> 00:32:24.980
and I'd have nothing left
to bargain with.

486
00:32:24.980 --> 00:32:28.610
- What were you bargain for?
- What do you think?

487
00:32:30.210 --> 00:32:31.070
(WHISPERS) You.

488
00:32:31.080 --> 00:32:33.310
I had to find a way to save you.

489
00:32:33.320 --> 00:32:34.490
I knew it had
to be the Time Lords.

490
00:32:34.490 --> 00:32:36.320
They cost you your life
on Trap Street. Clara.

491
00:32:36.320 --> 00:32:38.560
And I was gonna make them
bring you back.

492
00:32:38.560 --> 00:32:41.430
I just had to hang on
in there for a bit.

493
00:32:41.690 --> 00:32:44.650
- How long?
- It was fine.

494
00:32:48.570 --> 00:32:49.630
One question...

495
00:32:49.630 --> 00:32:50.360
And you will answer.

496
00:32:50.370 --> 00:32:53.340
How long was
the Doctor trapped inside
the confession dial?

497
00:32:53.340 --> 00:32:58.040
We think four-and-a-half
billion years.

498
00:32:58.040 --> 00:33:00.440
FEMALE GENERAL:
He could have left
anytime he wanted.

499
00:33:00.440 --> 00:33:02.140
He just had to say what he knew.

500
00:33:02.150 --> 00:33:04.720
The dial would have
released him.

501
00:33:11.690 --> 00:33:13.730
(BEEPING)

502
00:33:19.530 --> 00:33:22.670
(SOFTLY)
Four-and-a-half billion years?

503
00:33:23.700 --> 00:33:26.500
- If she says so.
- No.

504
00:33:28.170 --> 00:33:30.530
Why would you even do that?

505
00:33:31.180 --> 00:33:32.610
I was dead.

506
00:33:32.610 --> 00:33:34.210
I was dead and gone. Why?

507
00:33:34.210 --> 00:33:38.210
Why would you even
do that to yourself? (SIGHS)

508
00:33:40.990 --> 00:33:42.990
I had a duty of care.

509
00:33:44.390 --> 00:33:47.020
Listen. I'm nearly through here.

510
00:33:47.020 --> 00:33:48.250
(BEEPING)

511
00:33:48.260 --> 00:33:51.500
If I'm right. There should be
a service duct under here.

512
00:33:51.500 --> 00:33:54.030
We'll be able to get
to the Old Workshops.

513
00:33:54.030 --> 00:33:55.190
They'll have Tardises.

514
00:33:55.200 --> 00:33:58.440
- (SNIFFS) OK. listen.
- (HATCH DOOR OPENS)

515
00:33:58.440 --> 00:33:59.570
I have something I need to say.

516
00:33:59.570 --> 00:34:03.210
- We do not have time.
- No. my time...

517
00:34:04.710 --> 00:34:06.940
My time is up. Doctor.

518
00:34:06.940 --> 00:34:11.010
Between one heartbeat
and the last
is all the time I have.

519
00:34:12.750 --> 00:34:15.250
People like me and you...

520
00:34:15.250 --> 00:34:17.510
We should say things
to one another.

521
00:34:17.520 --> 00:34:20.280
CLARA: And I'm gonna
say them now.

522
00:34:42.380 --> 00:34:44.420
You're monsters.

523
00:34:44.680 --> 00:34:45.680
Here you are.

524
00:34:45.680 --> 00:34:48.040
Hiding away at the end of time.

525
00:34:48.050 --> 00:34:50.150
Do you even know why?

526
00:34:50.590 --> 00:34:52.660
Because you are hated.

527
00:34:53.590 --> 00:34:58.430
You are hated!

528
00:34:59.130 --> 00:35:00.400
By everybody.

529
00:35:00.400 --> 00:35:01.670
But by nobody more than me.

530
00:35:01.670 --> 00:35:04.000
- What did you say to him?
- (DOOR BEEPING)

531
00:35:04.000 --> 00:35:06.160
Oh. nothing I'm gonna tell you.

532
00:35:06.170 --> 00:35:08.210
Or anybody else.

533
00:35:08.340 --> 00:35:10.740
Except maybe this one part.

534
00:35:10.740 --> 00:35:12.700
I said...

535
00:35:15.580 --> 00:35:18.180
(WHISPERS)
"Don't worry. Doctor."

536
00:35:19.050 --> 00:35:21.290
"They'll all be
looking at me."

537
00:35:23.350 --> 00:35:26.280
You need to tell us what
the Doctor is going to do now.

538
00:35:26.290 --> 00:35:28.590
You really are thick.
aren't you?

539
00:35:28.590 --> 00:35:30.520
The Doctor is back on Gallifrey.

540
00:35:30.530 --> 00:35:34.770
Took him four-and-a-half
billion years to get here.

541
00:35:35.100 --> 00:35:37.270
What do you think
he's gonna do now?

542
00:35:37.270 --> 00:35:38.340
(WHOOSHING)

543
00:35:38.340 --> 00:35:42.370
Well. he's stealing a Tardis
and running away.

544
00:35:42.370 --> 00:35:44.430
Bye.

545
00:35:45.210 --> 00:35:46.210
CLARA: You were quick!

546
00:35:46.210 --> 00:35:48.180
Time machine. I backed up a bit.

547
00:35:48.180 --> 00:35:51.250
OHILA: <i>Doctor.
Doctor. face me!</i>

548
00:35:51.250 --> 00:35:52.520
Doctor. can you hear me?

549
00:35:52.520 --> 00:35:55.550
<i>Get out of that Tardis
and face me. boy.</i>

550
00:35:55.550 --> 00:35:58.210
- Boy?
- (BEEPING)

551
00:36:00.760 --> 00:36:01.690
OHILA: You have gone too far.

552
00:36:01.690 --> 00:36:04.550
You have broken every code
you ever lived by.

553
00:36:04.560 --> 00:36:08.260
After all this time.
after everything I've done.

554
00:36:08.270 --> 00:36:10.400
Don't you think the universe
owes me this?

555
00:36:10.400 --> 00:36:11.000
Owes you what?

556
00:36:11.000 --> 00:36:12.660
All you're doing
is giving her hope?

557
00:36:12.670 --> 00:36:14.240
Since when is hope a bad thing?

558
00:36:14.240 --> 00:36:19.110
Hope is a terrible thing
on the scaffold.

559
00:36:23.050 --> 00:36:25.020
(TARDIS WHOOSHING)

560
00:36:25.020 --> 00:36:26.550
(GRUNTS)

561
00:36:28.020 --> 00:36:29.460
WRAITH: Where can he run?

562
00:36:29.460 --> 00:36:31.750
Where he always runs.

563
00:36:31.760 --> 00:36:33.290
Away.

564
00:36:34.530 --> 00:36:37.200
Just away.

565
00:36:38.460 --> 00:36:39.720
What do you think
of the new wheels?

566
00:36:39.730 --> 00:36:42.130
- Basic.
- Classic.
Look at the colour scheme.

567
00:36:42.130 --> 00:36:44.590
- (CHUCKLES) It's all white.
- Genius!

568
00:36:44.600 --> 00:36:46.260
(THUD)

569
00:36:46.270 --> 00:36:48.170
Check your heartbeat again.

570
00:36:48.310 --> 00:36:51.110
- I think that you'll find
you have one.
- Yeah?

571
00:36:51.110 --> 00:36:55.750
It should've restarted
when we broke free
of Gallifrey's time zone.

572
00:36:56.750 --> 00:36:57.620
You're alive!

573
00:36:57.620 --> 00:36:59.710
Now. we just have to shake off
the Time Lords.

574
00:36:59.720 --> 00:37:01.550
There's only place
we can do that.

575
00:37:01.550 --> 00:37:03.350
What do say to lunch
followed by breakfast.

576
00:37:03.350 --> 00:37:05.920
because we're time-travellers
and that's how we roll?

577
00:37:05.920 --> 00:37:07.620
Then cocktails with Moses.

578
00:37:07.620 --> 00:37:09.550
Then I'm going to invent
a flying submarine. Why?

579
00:37:09.560 --> 00:37:11.660
Because no one ever has.
and it's annoying!

580
00:37:11.660 --> 00:37:14.390
And maybe we should
use this Tardis to find
my proper one.

581
00:37:14.400 --> 00:37:16.670
I need to change my shirt.

582
00:37:18.640 --> 00:37:20.040
Doctor!

583
00:37:20.200 --> 00:37:21.660
I still don't have a pulse.

584
00:37:21.670 --> 00:37:22.970
Oh. you just haven't
found it yet.

585
00:37:22.970 --> 00:37:24.530
- Try again.
- I know how to take my pulse.

586
00:37:24.540 --> 00:37:28.170
- (SIGHS)
- Look. I know how to do it.

587
00:37:29.380 --> 00:37:31.150
See. no pulse. right?

588
00:37:31.350 --> 00:37:34.390
- Uh-huh.
- (GLASSES WHIRRING)

589
00:37:37.390 --> 00:37:39.990
Is it still there?
Don't lie to me.

590
00:37:39.990 --> 00:37:42.700
Uh. maybe we just have to fly
a little bit farther.

591
00:37:42.700 --> 00:37:45.450
Give it a bit more welly.

592
00:37:49.300 --> 00:37:50.100
They said. your lot...

593
00:37:50.100 --> 00:37:53.240
That if you save me.
time would fracture.
What does that mean?

594
00:37:53.240 --> 00:37:56.210
Ah. they were just exaggerating.

595
00:37:56.210 --> 00:37:58.610
They exaggerate all the time.

596
00:37:58.610 --> 00:38:00.980
History will be fine.

597
00:38:00.980 --> 00:38:03.510
Time will heal.
It always does.

598
00:38:03.510 --> 00:38:04.670
- Always?
- Yeah.

599
00:38:04.680 --> 00:38:07.310
It'll sort itself out.
It'll be all right.

600
00:38:07.320 --> 00:38:10.990
You'll have a heartbeat.
Or don't you trust me
any more?

601
00:38:11.660 --> 00:38:14.330
No. Not when you're shouting.

602
00:38:21.270 --> 00:38:24.500
- Where are we going?
- Nowhere in space.

603
00:38:25.100 --> 00:38:26.930
Forward in time.

604
00:38:27.600 --> 00:38:30.270
We're going to the last hours
of the universe.

605
00:38:30.270 --> 00:38:34.700
We're going long past where
the Time Lords were hiding.

606
00:38:34.710 --> 00:38:36.640
Literally. to the end.

607
00:38:36.650 --> 00:38:39.420
They won't be able
to track us there.

608
00:38:39.420 --> 00:38:41.520
We'll just be there
for a minute.

609
00:38:41.520 --> 00:38:43.760
I just need to...

610
00:38:45.690 --> 00:38:48.330
I need to make an adjustment.

611
00:38:48.330 --> 00:38:49.130
To what?

612
00:38:49.130 --> 00:38:51.130
It's nothing. really.
It's this...

613
00:38:51.130 --> 00:38:55.570
A neural block?
Human compatible.
that's what you said.

614
00:39:00.540 --> 00:39:02.370
We don't have to stay here long.

615
00:39:02.370 --> 00:39:04.330
Uh. check your heartbeat again.

616
00:39:04.340 --> 00:39:08.070
Your timeline must have
started by now.

617
00:39:08.510 --> 00:39:10.070
Pulse. yeah?

618
00:39:11.080 --> 00:39:13.240
You have a pulse. yes?

619
00:39:13.550 --> 00:39:15.320
Pulse? Let me do it.

620
00:39:15.320 --> 00:39:19.060
- I am checking it properly.
- This should work.

621
00:39:19.420 --> 00:39:21.250
This has got to work.

622
00:39:21.260 --> 00:39:25.030
CLARA: What if one last
heartbeat is all I've got.

623
00:39:25.700 --> 00:39:27.360
What if time isn't healing?

624
00:39:27.360 --> 00:39:29.190
What if the universe
needs me to die?

625
00:39:29.200 --> 00:39:31.940
The universe is over!
It doesn't have
a say any more!

626
00:39:31.940 --> 00:39:33.740
We're standing
on the last ember.

627
00:39:33.740 --> 00:39:36.580
The last fragment
of everything that ever was.

628
00:39:36.580 --> 00:39:40.500
As of this moment.
I'm answerable to no one!

629
00:39:48.250 --> 00:39:49.280
(SIGHS)

630
00:39:49.290 --> 00:39:51.190
(KNOCKING ON DOOR)

631
00:39:54.760 --> 00:39:56.630
How can there be anybody there?

632
00:39:56.630 --> 00:39:58.200
(KNOCKING CONTINUES)

633
00:39:58.200 --> 00:40:00.130
Four knocks.

634
00:40:01.130 --> 00:40:03.430
It's always four knocks.

635
00:40:04.500 --> 00:40:05.760
No.

636
00:40:06.470 --> 00:40:08.270
This one. I do alone.

637
00:40:08.270 --> 00:40:10.370
What's out there?

638
00:40:11.170 --> 00:40:12.700
Me.

639
00:40:15.080 --> 00:40:17.220
(WHIRRING)

640
00:40:28.760 --> 00:40:31.200
I told you once...

641
00:40:32.260 --> 00:40:34.420
so long ago...

642
00:40:35.700 --> 00:40:41.210
That the universe would become
a very small place
when I'm angry with you.

643
00:40:43.040 --> 00:40:45.310
Small enough for you yet?

644
00:40:47.180 --> 00:40:49.180
Hello. me.

645
00:40:49.350 --> 00:40:51.820
You don't seem surprised
to see me.

646
00:40:53.750 --> 00:40:55.420
DOCTOR:
At the end of everything
we should expect

647
00:40:55.420 --> 00:40:58.690
the company of immortals.
so I've been told.

648
00:40:59.160 --> 00:41:01.660
Even the other immortals
are gone.

649
00:41:02.490 --> 00:41:04.220
It's just me.

650
00:41:05.030 --> 00:41:06.960
The one and only me.

651
00:41:06.960 --> 00:41:07.660
Finally. you earned the title.

652
00:41:07.660 --> 00:41:10.630
Sitting here
in a reality bubble
at the end of time itself.

653
00:41:10.630 --> 00:41:13.300
How are you sustaining it.
by the way?

654
00:41:13.740 --> 00:41:15.470
Brilliantly.

655
00:41:16.270 --> 00:41:18.600
I've been watching stars die.

656
00:41:19.680 --> 00:41:21.510
It was beautiful.

657
00:41:25.180 --> 00:41:26.680
No.

658
00:41:27.550 --> 00:41:29.110
It was sad.

659
00:41:29.120 --> 00:41:30.520
No.

660
00:41:30.520 --> 00:41:32.190
It was both.

661
00:41:32.190 --> 00:41:36.060
But that's not something
you'd understand. is it?

662
00:41:36.690 --> 00:41:39.220
You don't like endings.

663
00:41:40.260 --> 00:41:42.420
She died. Doctor.

664
00:41:43.000 --> 00:41:46.370
Clara died
billions of years ago.

665
00:41:46.370 --> 00:41:47.410
- You killed her.
- No.

666
00:41:47.410 --> 00:41:50.100
- You let it happen.
- No. I didn't.

667
00:41:50.110 --> 00:41:51.710
Neither did you.

668
00:41:51.710 --> 00:41:53.080
She did.

669
00:41:53.080 --> 00:41:55.780
She died for who she was
and for who she loved.

670
00:41:55.780 --> 00:41:59.050
She fell where she stood...
It was sad.

671
00:41:59.050 --> 00:42:01.290
And it was beautiful.

672
00:42:02.550 --> 00:42:03.580
And it is over.

673
00:42:03.590 --> 00:42:06.560
We have no right to change
who she was.

674
00:42:06.560 --> 00:42:08.330
- Ashildr.
- Me.

675
00:42:08.330 --> 00:42:09.030
Me. go to hell.

676
00:42:09.030 --> 00:42:12.760
By my calculations.
you've got about five minutes.

677
00:42:13.160 --> 00:42:15.220
You know why we run. Doctor?

678
00:42:15.230 --> 00:42:15.960
Because it's fun.

679
00:42:15.970 --> 00:42:19.300
Because we know
summer can't last forever.

680
00:42:19.300 --> 00:42:20.630
(WHISPERS) Of course. it can.

681
00:42:20.640 --> 00:42:22.770
Of course. it can.

682
00:42:22.770 --> 00:42:25.230
You just have to steal
a time machine.

683
00:42:25.240 --> 00:42:26.740
The Hybrid.

684
00:42:27.780 --> 00:42:31.480
Five minutes to hell.
I think it's time
to tell the truth.

685
00:42:31.480 --> 00:42:33.410
(BEEPING)

686
00:42:47.260 --> 00:42:47.690
Screen on.

687
00:42:47.700 --> 00:42:50.540
ASHILDR: <i>You were barely
more than a child.</i>

688
00:42:50.540 --> 00:42:51.790
<i>You broke in here.</i>

689
00:42:51.800 --> 00:42:54.130
<i>And the Wraith spoke to you
about the Hybrid.</i>

690
00:42:54.140 --> 00:42:55.610
<i>Why did that story
make you so scared?</i>

691
00:42:55.610 --> 00:42:58.140
DOCTOR: <i>I don't know.
I don't remember everything.</i>

692
00:42:58.140 --> 00:42:59.700
(CHUCKLES) Sometimes you do.

693
00:42:59.710 --> 00:43:02.150
It's always the way
with things
we'd rather forget.

694
00:43:02.150 --> 00:43:04.050
You remember now
though. don't you?

695
00:43:04.050 --> 00:43:06.980
Tell me. Doctor.
who is the Hybrid?

696
00:43:06.980 --> 00:43:09.080
Who threatens
all of time and space?

697
00:43:09.090 --> 00:43:11.690
Oh. that's easy.
That's very. very easy.

698
00:43:11.690 --> 00:43:13.990
The Hybrid...

699
00:43:14.490 --> 00:43:16.020
is you.

700
00:43:16.190 --> 00:43:19.290
ASHILDR:
I'm human. with a little bit
of Mire inside me.

701
00:43:19.300 --> 00:43:22.470
The Hybrid is supposed to be
half Time Lord. half Dalek.

702
00:43:22.470 --> 00:43:23.200
DOCTOR: No. it isn't.

703
00:43:23.200 --> 00:43:26.100
The actual prophecy specifies
only two warrior races.

704
00:43:26.100 --> 00:43:29.530
The Daleks and the Time Lords
have made assumptions.
of course.

705
00:43:29.540 --> 00:43:30.770
And they would.

706
00:43:30.770 --> 00:43:34.000
Humans and the Mire.

707
00:43:34.010 --> 00:43:37.150
Both warrior races.
fits perfectly.

708
00:43:37.610 --> 00:43:40.010
It's an interesting theory.

709
00:43:40.450 --> 00:43:42.420
Do you have a better one?

710
00:43:42.520 --> 00:43:44.050
By your own reasoning.

711
00:43:44.050 --> 00:43:49.120
why couldn't the Hybrid be
half Time Lord. half human?

712
00:43:51.060 --> 00:43:55.390
Tell me. Doctor.
I've always wondered.
You're a Time Lord...

713
00:43:55.400 --> 00:43:58.130
You're a highborn Gallifryean.

714
00:43:58.130 --> 00:44:01.460
Why is it you spend
so much time on Earth?

715
00:44:03.370 --> 00:44:05.000
That's your best theory?
I'm the Hybrid?

716
00:44:05.010 --> 00:44:08.450
I've run away from Gallifrey
because I was
afraid of myself?

717
00:44:08.450 --> 00:44:10.280
It doesn't make any sense.

718
00:44:10.280 --> 00:44:13.590
It makes perfect sense.
and you know it.

719
00:44:14.220 --> 00:44:16.190
ASHILDR: Am I right?

720
00:44:17.050 --> 00:44:18.380
Is it true?

721
00:44:18.390 --> 00:44:20.190
Does it matter?

722
00:44:22.630 --> 00:44:24.260
No.

723
00:44:25.430 --> 00:44:28.330
Because I have a better theory.

724
00:44:28.630 --> 00:44:29.120
Really?

725
00:44:29.130 --> 00:44:34.330
What if the Hybrid
wasn't one person. but two?

726
00:44:37.110 --> 00:44:39.380
- Two?
- A dangerous combination...

727
00:44:39.380 --> 00:44:42.250
of a passionate
and powerful Time Lord.

728
00:44:42.250 --> 00:44:44.680
and a young woman.
so very similar to him.

729
00:44:44.680 --> 00:44:48.640
Companions who are willing to
push each other to extremes.

730
00:44:48.650 --> 00:44:52.250
She's my friend.
She's just my friend.

731
00:44:52.260 --> 00:44:54.490
ASHILDR: How did you meet her?

732
00:44:55.060 --> 00:44:56.430
Missy?

733
00:44:57.190 --> 00:44:58.650
Missy.

734
00:44:59.000 --> 00:45:02.070
Missy. the Master.

735
00:45:03.170 --> 00:45:05.340
The lover of chaos.

736
00:45:05.400 --> 00:45:07.200
Who wants you to love it. too.

737
00:45:07.200 --> 00:45:09.360
She's quite the matchmaker.

738
00:45:10.070 --> 00:45:12.000
Clara's my friend.

739
00:45:12.010 --> 00:45:12.640
I know.

740
00:45:12.640 --> 00:45:18.540
And you're willing to risk
all of time and space
because you miss her.

741
00:45:18.550 --> 00:45:22.150
One wonders
what the pair of you
will get up to next.

742
00:45:22.150 --> 00:45:24.950
Nothing. Nothing at all.

743
00:45:24.950 --> 00:45:27.220
I know I went too far.

744
00:45:27.220 --> 00:45:28.220
I get it.

745
00:45:28.220 --> 00:45:31.120
That's why I'm doing
what I'm doing.

746
00:45:31.130 --> 00:45:32.260
And what would that be?

747
00:45:32.260 --> 00:45:33.120
I'm taking her back to Earth.

748
00:45:33.130 --> 00:45:35.330
Somewhere safe.
somewhere out of the way.

749
00:45:35.330 --> 00:45:39.630
I'm going to wipe her memory
of every last detail of me.

750
00:45:39.640 --> 00:45:42.010
<i>It'll be like our friendship
never happened.</i>

751
00:45:42.010 --> 00:45:44.240
ASHILDR: <i>That may not be
what she wants.</i>

752
00:45:44.240 --> 00:45:46.780
DOCTOR: <i>I've done it before.</i>

753
00:45:46.780 --> 00:45:48.480
<i>Usually. I do it telepathically.</i>

754
00:45:48.480 --> 00:45:52.020
<i>But this time.
I've got something better.</i>

755
00:45:53.520 --> 00:45:57.190
(SOFTLY) It's quite painless.

756
00:45:57.190 --> 00:45:59.320
Will you tell her
what you're going to do?

757
00:45:59.320 --> 00:46:02.350
- Of course.
- When?

758
00:46:02.660 --> 00:46:04.260
Now.

759
00:46:07.960 --> 00:46:11.130
- Screen off.
- (MONITOR BEEPING)

760
00:46:23.550 --> 00:46:25.010
You OK?

761
00:46:25.010 --> 00:46:26.140
CLARA: Yeah.

762
00:46:26.150 --> 00:46:28.750
Yeah. yeah.
Just. you know. my pulse.

763
00:46:28.750 --> 00:46:30.950
Yeah. we'll fix that somehow.
I promise.

764
00:46:30.950 --> 00:46:33.320
You remember Ashildr. of course.

765
00:46:33.320 --> 00:46:35.080
Yeah. sure.

766
00:46:35.630 --> 00:46:38.400
I thought you'd be more
surprised to see her?

767
00:46:41.060 --> 00:46:42.460
I was watching.

768
00:46:43.400 --> 00:46:45.340
On the monitor.

769
00:46:45.700 --> 00:46:47.230
(GASPS) No.

770
00:46:47.240 --> 00:46:50.640
Doctor.
whatever you're about to do.
don't do it.

771
00:46:50.640 --> 00:46:52.010
It won't hurt. it'll be nothing.

772
00:46:52.010 --> 00:46:53.210
- You will just pass out
for a moment.
- And then?

773
00:46:53.210 --> 00:46:56.110
- When you wake.
you will be fine.
- But...

774
00:46:56.110 --> 00:46:58.370
- Clara. just listen to me...
- Just say it.

775
00:46:58.380 --> 00:47:00.610
Say it. come on. Tell me.

776
00:47:00.620 --> 00:47:02.920
When you wake up.
you will have forgotten me.

777
00:47:02.920 --> 00:47:04.650
You will have forgotten
we ever even met.

778
00:47:04.650 --> 00:47:06.010
And why would I want that?

779
00:47:06.020 --> 00:47:07.050
Because it's the only way...

780
00:47:07.060 --> 00:47:09.190
That stuff in your head.
the image of me...

781
00:47:09.190 --> 00:47:11.420
They could use it to find you.

782
00:47:11.430 --> 00:47:13.400
I. uh... I used these.

783
00:47:13.400 --> 00:47:14.370
- On what?
- That.

784
00:47:14.370 --> 00:47:16.190
- What did you do?
- What do you think?

785
00:47:16.200 --> 00:47:18.370
Ashildr's right. you see.
We're too alike.

786
00:47:18.370 --> 00:47:19.370
- Tell me what you did.
- What else?

787
00:47:19.370 --> 00:47:21.270
What else do you think I did?
I reversed the polarity.

788
00:47:21.270 --> 00:47:24.000
Push that button. Doctor.
it will go off in your
own face.

789
00:47:24.010 --> 00:47:26.580
- Are you trying to trick me?
- What are you
trying to do to me?

790
00:47:26.580 --> 00:47:29.610
- I'm trying to keep you safe.
- Why?

791
00:47:30.510 --> 00:47:32.110
Nobody's ever safe...

792
00:47:32.120 --> 00:47:34.580
I've never asked you for that.
ever.

793
00:47:34.580 --> 00:47:37.150
These have been
the best years of my life.

794
00:47:37.150 --> 00:47:39.110
And they are mine.

795
00:47:39.290 --> 00:47:44.030
Tomorrow's promised
to no one. Doctor.
but I insist upon my past.

796
00:47:44.030 --> 00:47:46.230
I am entitled to that.

797
00:47:47.730 --> 00:47:49.470
It's mine.

798
00:47:59.540 --> 00:48:02.440
Oh. Clara Oswald.

799
00:48:05.220 --> 00:48:07.150
What am I doing?

800
00:48:12.190 --> 00:48:14.090
You're right.

801
00:48:15.430 --> 00:48:17.560
You're always...

802
00:48:17.560 --> 00:48:19.530
Always right.

803
00:48:22.170 --> 00:48:25.440
So what happens now? Eh?

804
00:48:25.440 --> 00:48:27.570
Me and you. what do we do now?

805
00:48:27.570 --> 00:48:29.610
I'm not sure you managed
to reverse the polarity.

806
00:48:29.610 --> 00:48:33.010
I'm not even sure that you can.

807
00:48:34.580 --> 00:48:36.480
It'll do something.

808
00:48:36.980 --> 00:48:38.410
To one of us.

809
00:48:38.410 --> 00:48:40.610
Better than flipping a coin.

810
00:48:41.550 --> 00:48:43.350
Doctor...

811
00:48:45.220 --> 00:48:47.750
You and me. together.

812
00:48:50.060 --> 00:48:52.160
Look how far I went.

813
00:48:52.560 --> 00:48:54.660
For fear of losing you.

814
00:48:56.630 --> 00:48:58.630
This has to stop.

815
00:48:58.700 --> 00:49:00.760
One of us has to go.

816
00:49:14.550 --> 00:49:16.650
You really don't know which?

817
00:49:16.650 --> 00:49:18.410
Let's find out.

818
00:49:19.460 --> 00:49:20.520
Let's do it.

819
00:49:20.520 --> 00:49:23.290
Like we've done
everything else...

820
00:49:24.590 --> 00:49:26.320
Together.

821
00:49:29.430 --> 00:49:31.030
How about we just don't?

822
00:49:31.030 --> 00:49:33.530
Why don't we just
fly away somewhere?

823
00:49:33.540 --> 00:49:37.740
- Oh. that'd be great.
wouldn't it?
-(BOTH CHUCKLE)

824
00:49:40.580 --> 00:49:42.280
God. yeah.

825
00:49:42.280 --> 00:49:43.550
(LAUGHS)

826
00:49:45.680 --> 00:49:47.710
Good luck. Clara.

827
00:49:48.420 --> 00:49:50.520
Good luck. Doctor.

828
00:49:51.590 --> 00:49:53.660
(BEEPING)

829
00:49:56.190 --> 00:49:58.220
So. what happens now?

830
00:50:01.160 --> 00:50:04.560
I suppose we just. um...
We just wait a minute.
I suppose.

831
00:50:04.570 --> 00:50:06.300
One of us...

832
00:50:12.080 --> 00:50:13.750
One of us...

833
00:50:15.110 --> 00:50:18.070
I don't think
I could ever forget you.

834
00:50:20.780 --> 00:50:24.280
Clara. I don't think
you're ever gonna have to.

835
00:50:26.220 --> 00:50:28.050
(CLATTERS)

836
00:50:30.230 --> 00:50:31.630
(GASPS)

837
00:50:32.600 --> 00:50:34.000
No...

838
00:50:34.400 --> 00:50:36.800
- Run like hell.
- What?

839
00:50:37.230 --> 00:50:38.630
Run like hell because
you always need to.

840
00:50:38.630 --> 00:50:41.560
Laugh at everything
because it's always funny.

841
00:50:41.570 --> 00:50:43.530
No. stop it.
you're saying goodbye.

842
00:50:43.540 --> 00:50:44.510
Don't say goodbye!

843
00:50:44.510 --> 00:50:47.240
Never be cruel
and never be cowardly.

844
00:50:47.240 --> 00:50:51.410
And if you ever are.
always make amends.

845
00:50:51.410 --> 00:50:53.380
- (GASPS)
- Stop it!

846
00:50:53.380 --> 00:50:55.140
Stop this... Stop it!

847
00:50:55.150 --> 00:50:57.650
Never eat pears.
they're too squishy.

848
00:50:57.650 --> 00:50:58.710
And they always make
your chin wet.

849
00:50:58.720 --> 00:51:00.620
That one is quite important.
write it down.

850
00:51:00.620 --> 00:51:02.950
I didn't mean to do this.
I'm sorry.

851
00:51:02.960 --> 00:51:05.500
It's OK. (GROANS)

852
00:51:06.000 --> 00:51:07.530
It's OK.

853
00:51:08.430 --> 00:51:10.190
I went too far.

854
00:51:10.200 --> 00:51:12.170
I broke all my own rules.

855
00:51:12.170 --> 00:51:14.570
I became the Hybrid.

856
00:51:14.570 --> 00:51:16.470
This is right!

857
00:51:16.470 --> 00:51:18.300
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

858
00:51:18.310 --> 00:51:20.210
I accept it.

859
00:51:21.110 --> 00:51:22.680
I can't.

860
00:51:24.610 --> 00:51:27.710
There has to be something
I can do.

861
00:51:29.150 --> 00:51:30.680
Smile for me.

862
00:51:31.190 --> 00:51:34.330
Go on. Clara Oswald.

863
00:51:34.760 --> 00:51:36.730
One last time.

864
00:51:39.160 --> 00:51:41.160
How could I smile?

865
00:51:44.770 --> 00:51:46.470
It's OK.

866
00:51:46.770 --> 00:51:48.670
Don't you worry.

867
00:51:49.140 --> 00:51:51.180
(SOFTLY) I'll remember you.

868
00:52:09.660 --> 00:52:11.060
Sir.

869
00:52:11.630 --> 00:52:14.130
Are you all right?

870
00:52:15.530 --> 00:52:17.360
Where am I?

871
00:52:21.270 --> 00:52:22.640
How did I get here?

872
00:52:22.640 --> 00:52:24.580
Clara asked me
to look after you.

873
00:52:24.580 --> 00:52:27.700
She said you might be
a bit upset.

874
00:52:28.480 --> 00:52:30.210
- Clara?
- Yeah.

875
00:52:30.210 --> 00:52:32.270
She was just here.

876
00:52:32.680 --> 00:52:35.180
I don't know where she went.

877
00:52:36.320 --> 00:52:37.790
Clara?

878
00:52:38.550 --> 00:52:40.320
Clara. who?

879
00:52:40.490 --> 00:52:46.460
When something goes missing.
you can always recreate it
by the hole it left.

880
00:52:47.000 --> 00:52:49.200
I know her name was Clara.

881
00:52:49.200 --> 00:52:50.770
I know we travelled together.

882
00:52:50.770 --> 00:52:55.640
I know that there was
an Ice Warrior on a submarine.
a Mummy on the Orient Express

883
00:52:55.640 --> 00:52:58.310
I know we sat together
in the Cloisters

884
00:52:58.310 --> 00:53:01.010
and she told me something
very important.

885
00:53:01.010 --> 00:53:03.210
but I've no idea what she said.

886
00:53:05.050 --> 00:53:07.120
Or what she looked like.

887
00:53:07.580 --> 00:53:09.610
Or how she talked.

888
00:53:10.150 --> 00:53:11.980
Or laughed.

889
00:53:14.760 --> 00:53:16.630
There's nothing there.

890
00:53:16.630 --> 00:53:18.360
Just nothing.

891
00:53:21.660 --> 00:53:23.590
Are you looking for her?

892
00:53:25.400 --> 00:53:27.300
I'm trying. (SIGHS)

893
00:53:27.440 --> 00:53:29.240
She could be anyone. right?

894
00:53:29.240 --> 00:53:32.040
You don't know
who you're looking for.
I mean...

895
00:53:32.040 --> 00:53:34.400
She could be me.
for all you know.

896
00:53:34.410 --> 00:53:36.780
There's one thing
I know about her.

897
00:53:36.780 --> 00:53:37.780
just one thing.

898
00:53:37.780 --> 00:53:41.450
If I met her again.
I'd absolutely know her.

899
00:53:43.320 --> 00:53:47.090
I think that we were here.
you know.

900
00:53:47.490 --> 00:53:50.600
I think that we were
here together once.

901
00:53:51.060 --> 00:53:53.130
I'm sure I remember.

902
00:53:54.260 --> 00:53:56.090
Over here.

903
00:53:58.070 --> 00:53:59.070
Stupid...

904
00:53:59.070 --> 00:54:02.370
Amy and Rory.
It was Amy and Rory.

905
00:54:03.640 --> 00:54:05.980
What about your Tardis. eh?

906
00:54:05.980 --> 00:54:07.940
- You found that yet?
- No.

907
00:54:07.940 --> 00:54:11.710
Somebody's moved it
from London.
I'm still looking.

908
00:54:13.150 --> 00:54:15.020
This diner...

909
00:54:16.020 --> 00:54:17.950
It wasn't always here. was it?

910
00:54:17.950 --> 00:54:19.650
It used to be
on the other side of the hill.

911
00:54:19.660 --> 00:54:23.130
Maybe someone
will find your Tardis for you.

912
00:54:28.330 --> 00:54:30.460
(GUITAR STRUMMING)

913
00:54:39.510 --> 00:54:42.580
What Clara told you
in the Cloisters...

914
00:54:44.150 --> 00:54:46.350
I don't remember
a single thing about it...

915
00:54:46.350 --> 00:54:48.180
You said. "Memories..."

916
00:54:48.180 --> 00:54:52.210
"become stories
when we forget them."

917
00:54:53.690 --> 00:54:56.590
Maybe some of them become songs.

918
00:54:57.330 --> 00:54:59.300
(GUITAR STRUMMING)

919
00:54:59.300 --> 00:55:01.130
That'd be nice.

920
00:55:05.230 --> 00:55:07.960
Yeah. it would be. wouldn't it?

921
00:55:24.720 --> 00:55:27.390
(TARDIS WHOOSHING)

922
00:55:33.600 --> 00:55:35.970
(WIND WHISTLING)

923
00:55:51.550 --> 00:55:54.650
ASHILDR: I don't think
I've got the chameleon
circuit working.

924
00:55:54.650 --> 00:55:58.290
The outer shell might be stuck
as an American diner.

925
00:55:58.290 --> 00:55:59.520
Awesome.

926
00:56:00.160 --> 00:56:01.530
Still no pulse?

927
00:56:02.530 --> 00:56:03.590
(SNIFFS)

928
00:56:03.590 --> 00:56:07.190
Time isn't healing.
I'm still frozen.

929
00:56:07.200 --> 00:56:08.070
You know what that means?

930
00:56:08.070 --> 00:56:10.430
It means my death
is a fixed event.

931
00:56:10.430 --> 00:56:13.290
The universe
depends on it happening.

932
00:56:13.300 --> 00:56:14.630
I'm sorry.

933
00:56:14.640 --> 00:56:15.410
Why?

934
00:56:15.410 --> 00:56:17.530
Why does everybody think
I am so scared?

935
00:56:17.540 --> 00:56:21.180
We all face the Raven
in the end.
That is the deal.

936
00:56:21.180 --> 00:56:23.650
If I go back to Gallifrey.
they can put me back. right?

937
00:56:23.650 --> 00:56:26.420
On Trap Street.
the moment they took me out?

938
00:56:26.420 --> 00:56:28.020
Of course.

939
00:56:29.250 --> 00:56:31.080
Mind you.

940
00:56:31.290 --> 00:56:32.360
seeing as I'm
not actually ageing.

941
00:56:32.360 --> 00:56:35.360
there's still a tiny
little bit of wiggle room.
isn't there?

942
00:56:35.360 --> 00:56:38.190
- Wiggle room?
- Wiggle room. yeah.

943
00:56:38.190 --> 00:56:40.190
You know. wiggle room.

944
00:56:40.200 --> 00:56:44.270
We could. um. you know.
stop off on the way.

945
00:56:45.030 --> 00:56:47.300
- Where are we going?
- Gallifrey.

946
00:56:47.300 --> 00:56:49.400
Like I said...

947
00:56:50.610 --> 00:56:51.510
Gallifrey.

948
00:56:51.510 --> 00:56:53.780
- (CLICK)
- (TARDIS THUDS)

949
00:56:55.040 --> 00:56:56.740
The long way round.

950
00:57:30.710 --> 00:57:32.670
(DOOR CREAKS AND THUDS)

951
00:57:44.660 --> 00:57:46.660
(TARDIS POWERING UP)

952
00:58:40.580 --> 00:58:42.310
(WHIRRING)

953
00:58:47.660 --> 00:58:49.730
(DOOR CREAKS AND THUDS)

954
00:59:00.400 --> 00:59:01.260
(CLICKS)

955
00:59:01.270 --> 00:59:03.410
(TARDIS WHOOSHING)

956
00:59:14.580 --> 00:59:16.610
(RUSTLING)

957
00:59:23.090 --> 00:59:25.590
(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)

958
00:59:52.690 --> 00:59:54.190
(KNOCKING ON DOOR)

959
00:59:54.190 --> 00:59:55.990
Is there anything on my head?

960
00:59:55.990 --> 00:59:57.950
Erm... well. yes.

961
00:59:58.190 --> 01:00:01.220
River!
<i>Death initiating.</i>

962
01:00:01.230 --> 01:00:04.500
Stop holding my hand.
People don't do that
to me.

963
01:00:04.500 --> 01:00:05.730
Destroy them!

964
01:00:05.730 --> 01:00:08.060
RIVER: Nobody move!
Or the head gets it.

965
01:00:08.070 --> 01:00:11.380
Sonic Trowel?
Do you realize how
ridiculous that sounds?

966
01:00:12.310 --> 01:00:16.450
You planned to take my head?
Never crossed my mind.

967
01:00:16.450 --> 01:00:17.580
<i>Long live the King.</i>

968
01:00:17.580 --> 01:00:21.350
RIVER: This is a serious
mission. There is nothing
to laugh about here.

969
01:00:21.350 --> 01:00:23.390
We're being threatened by a bag!

970
01:00:23.390 --> 01:00:25.290
Give us the treasure!
